      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "please do this - there are no good reasons to limit the camera movement, while it restricts the creative freedom that we expect from VR, and often need to fulfill our vision.\n\nthe current limit isn't even \"good enough\" - i regularly hit the virtual wall without even trying to do anything crazy.\n\nthe only potential issue being privacy should be responded to with \"just go to a private world then\".\n\nyes, drone mode exists, and they can fly much much further, but they're locked behind VRC+, and are needlessly harder to control to simply take photos.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-03-10T14:40:58.847Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It's always sad or disappointing to discover that what you want to take a picture of can't be done because range limitations. If it's for performance, then why not set it on a toggle? Thanks for hearing me out. \n\nI have like two more requests so I hope you don't mind.",
